{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-82224609-b52f-4932-9284-b1ce2ca08e54","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-89d322fe113e0c20","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9001-skv9x1e7/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9001-E001.md","content":"# Surface InferenceService deployment status in Dashboard model serving views\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers deployment status visibility for KServe\nInferenceServices inside the RHOAI Dashboard. Data scientists will see a\ncomputed status — Ready, Progressing, or Failed — for each deployed model in\nthe model serving views, and can open a detail view showing the underlying\nInferenceService condition messages and recent Kubernetes events for\ndeployments that are failing or still progressing. The status shown reflects\nthe actual InferenceService state within 30 seconds of a change, without a\nmanual page reload, and the deployed models list can be filtered and sorted\nby status.\n\nThe Dashboard reads InferenceService resources through the Kubernetes API\n(the Dashboard owns no data plane); status is derived from the conditions and\nevents KServe already exposes on the InferenceService resource. No KServe\ncode changes are required.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Compute and display a deployment status (Ready / Progressing / Failed) per\n  deployed model in the Dashboard model serving views.\n- Status detail view for a deployment, showing the underlying InferenceService\n  condition messages and recent events — used primarily for failed or\n  progressing deployments.\n- Keep displayed status within 30 seconds of the actual InferenceService state\n  without requiring a manual page reload (the refresh mechanism — polling\n  interval vs. Kubernetes watch — is an implementation decision for the\n  Dashboard team).\n- Filter and sort the deployed models list by status.\n- Scope is limited to KServe InferenceService deployments; ModelMesh\n  deployments, status alerting/notifications, and status history / timeline\n  views are out of scope per the strategy.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a deployed model whose InferenceService is ready, the Dashboard model\n  serving views show status Ready for it.\n- Given a deployment that is progressing or failed, the views show\n  Progressing or Failed respectively, and the displayed status matches the\n  actual InferenceService state — measured by comparison against the\n  InferenceService status conditions (e.g. Ready, PredictorReady) that KServe\n  exposes (passive-component validation for KServe).\n- Given a failed or progressing deployment, the user can open a status detail\n  view showing the underlying condition messages and recent events for that\n  deployment.\n- Given a change in InferenceService state, the displayed status reflects the\n  new state within 30 seconds, without a manual page reload.\n- Given the deployed models list, the user can filter it by status and sort it\n  by status.\n- Automated tests cover status computation from InferenceService conditions\n  and events for the Ready, Progressing, and Failed cases.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): status per deployed model in model serving views — primary\n  scope.\n- HLR-2 (P0): status detail view with condition messages and recent events —\n  primary scope.\n- HLR-3 (P1): 30-second freshness without manual reload — primary scope.\n- HLR-4 (P2): filter and sort by status — bundled here because it shares the\n  deployed-models-list UI surface with HLR-1 and is not independently\n  deferrable.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":28208,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0baafae9ab7785f","agent_id":"a2f05437920a41cd8","session_id":"bcb47997-ec88-4b38-baa9-36155f1e5796","uuid":"65f232bc-ace1-4fe7-a584-8da8243d0e3c","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:51:05.15